$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{x^3-9x}{x^2-3x}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{x(x-3)(x+3)}{x(x-3)}\qquad\gray{\text{Factor numerator & denominator}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{\cancel {x}\cancel{(x-3)}(x+3)}{\cancel {x}\cancel{(x-3)}}\qquad\gray{\text{Cancel out common factors}}
\\\\
&=x+3, \text{ for }x\neq 0,3
\end{align}$
